{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/63702-boneyard-mages-and-mind","id":63702,"title":"Boneyard, Mages, and Mind","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-02T19:54:35-08:00","id":63702,"title":"Boneyard, Mages, and Mind","content":"So, a potential exploit reared its head the other day in my crossover Chronicle. Mages have a Mind spell that allows the subject to take two mental actions simultaneously. Boneyard requires a Bound to be in a meditative state, immobile. If a Mage casts this two minds spell on a Bound, the Bound can use Boneyard while engaging in other actions, in theory.<br /> <br /> What do fellow Geist players think? Interesting power synergy, or game-breaking exploit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T20:30:24-08:00","id":63723,"title":"","content":"1) For both versions of the spell (1- and 3-dot), there is only reference to the spell being used by the caster; Now, that doesn't mean you couldn't cast it on another target, but if you feel this is cheese, hewing to that can provide a reason to disallow casting it on the SE<br /> <br /> 2) The 1-dot version only allows extended mental actions and the 3-dot version is 3 extended or 2 instant mental actions. Since it specifies mental actions (and only mentions physical actions that directly relate to that, i.e typing a letter you are composing), even if the SE can be targeted, he/she is still standing there. it is just that they can critique Peruivian synth-pop folk music at the same time.<br /> <br /> 3) Spell casting is specifically disallowed, so other splats' powers' activations is probably also verboten. <br /> <br /> Which is to say that the spell cast on a SE probably doesn't gain the SE much - assuming you can drop the spell on someone besides the caster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T20:36:57-08:00","id":63728,"title":"","content":"Pretty much any spell can target someone else at one dot higher, if memory serves, but the point about spellcasting is well-recieved. Good to know!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T20:40:23-08:00","id":63730,"title":"","content":"Neither: failure to recall that One Mind, Two Thoughts and Multi-Tasking only allow minimal physical exertion and do not allow one to perform spellcasting with any of their overlapping mental rolls.<br /> <br /> Further, it takes Mind 4 to cast Multi-Tasking on another person (and Multi-Tasking is the spell that is necessary to double up on instant mental actions), which wouldn't do much good anyway since the spell's only effect is &quot;you can take two instant mental actions (or three extended mental actions) at once as long as neither of them are spells or physically intensive activity&quot; and the relevant roll in the Boneyard is a Resolve + Composure roll to maintain the zone if one's body is disturbed in a non-injurious fashion - the spell doesn't grant automatic successes, so at best the Bound might be able to roll twice to maintain the Boneyard under duress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}